Looking at the sequence trace and the code, I can see the issue is in the circular buffer eviction formula. When `writeIndex` is small (like 1) and we subtract `windowSize` (2), we get -1, and IEC 61131-3 MOD with negative numbers has implementation-defined behavior.

The correct formula should be `((writeIndex - 1) MOD windowSize) + 1` which always produces a non-negative intermediate value.

```json
{
  "edits": [
    {
      "old": "            tmpOldSlot := ((writeIndex - windowSize) MOD windowSize) + 1;",
      "new": "            tmpOldSlot := ((writeIndex - 1) MOD windowSize) + 1;"
    }
  ]
}
```
